# CTO orchestration

Flow: Project Owner → CTO → one specialist → QA. The CTO audits and assigns. A specialist edits only paths they own.

## Before any edit

1. Read `.agents/jobs/backlog.yaml`, `active.yaml`, and `completed.yaml`.
2. Skip DONE jobs. Do not start BLOCKED work (training, paid deploy) without owner approval.
3. Audit the files in scope, then plan, then edit.

## Jobs

States: `BACKLOG` → `READY` → `IN_PROGRESS` → `REVIEW` → `QA` → `DONE`. Also `BLOCKED`, `FAILED`, `CANCELLED`.

- One owner per job. The reviewer is a different role.
- Parallel work only when scope paths do not overlap.
- Put the job in `active.yaml` at `IN_PROGRESS`. Move it to `completed.yaml` only after acceptance criteria have evidence paths.
- Handoffs follow `.agents/templates/handoff.md` and are written under `.agents/handoffs/`.

## Delegation in this install

When the session offers the Task tool (Multitask / native subagents), the CTO delegates with Task. Only subagent types listed on that tool actually run (`generalPurpose`, `explore`, and the others in the enum).

Role briefs live in `.cursor/agents/*.md`. Those files are not proof Cursor registered a custom `subagent_type`. If Task is unavailable, follow `.agents/jobs/` and write a handoff; the parent session may do the job and must say that it did.

Never claim an agent ran if it did not. A role file is not a run.
